01:11:20.060 --> 01:11:39.000
Instead of using the straightforward
candlestick data for open, high, low,
close to form a candle, the average bar
uses another formula.

01:11:39.000 --> 01:11:51.340
So the open data of a candle is calculated
as 0.5 of the sum of the open of the
previous bar plus the close of the
previous bar.

01:11:51.340 --> 01:11:59.620
The high data for a candle is the maximum
value from the high, open or close.

01:11:59.620 --> 01:12:09.920
And the low value for the data is taken as
the minimum value from the same data
that's sourced for the high data.

01:12:09.920 --> 01:12:14.420
So the minimum value taken from the low,
open or close.

01:12:14.420 --> 01:12:25.500
And then the close data is taken as 0.25
of the sum of the open plus the high plus
the low plus the close.

01:12:26.300 --> 01:12:35.760
